            <ArticleTitle>Hyperventilation and myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1095-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chest pain that is associated with hyperventilation is often considered to be benign and noncardiac in nature. While not commonly recognized, hyperventilation can provoke coronary vasospasm. We report a man who presented with hyperventilation and developed myocardial infarction. In the setting of hyperventilation, chest pain and ST segment elevation, coronary vasospasm must be considered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
